abstract: >-
  RNBeamX is a browser-based designer for publication-ready figures of
  optical experiments and graphical abstracts. Optical parts placed on the
  page are traced live: reflection, splitting, refraction with dispersion and
  total internal reflection, ideal and real spherical-surface lenses,
  Gaussian beams, Jones-calculus polarisation, ghost reflections,
  interference, gratings, emission and nonlinear conversion. Ray bundles
  give imaging ray diagrams with spot-size and best-focus readouts. Device
  cross-sections built from stackable blocks are calculated with a
  transfer-matrix method or RCWA using measured optical constants. Figures
  are exported as SVG, PDF, PNG, TIFF, PowerPoint, TikZ or video, and all
  calculations run locally in the browser.
keywords:
